# The build context for dockerfiles/Dockerfile, which is the repository root so the image can
# take the game straight from the clone.
#
# Everything is excluded first and the few things the image needs are let back in. The rules after
# that re-inclusion are what matter, and they are kept in PARITY with the lists the project
# already maintains:
#
#   tools/updater/h9xash_updater.py   SKIP_DIR_NAMES, SKIP_DIR_PATHS, SKIP_NAMES, SKIP_EXT
#   .gitignore                        the H9XASH/** entries
#   stage-h9xash.ps1                  the same rules, for the shipped packages
#
# If you add a file to one of those, add it here too. Three groups matter and each is marked
# below: SECRETS (must never reach an image anyone might push), PLAYER FILES (belong to whoever
# runs the game, not to a release), and WINDOWS (dead weight in a Linux server image).
*

!H9XASH
!linux
!dockerfiles
!VERSION.txt

# The built 32-bit binaries, for H9_BINARIES=local. Git-ignored and only 44 MiB, and NOT covered
# by the !H9XASH line above: that pattern matches the folder named exactly H9XASH and its
# children, not a sibling whose name merely starts the same way.
!H9XASH-linux

# H9XASH-Updater, the Linux build (tools/updater/build-linux.sh writes it here). Build output like
# the binaries above and git-ignored with the rest of dist/, so a clone has it only when somebody
# has built it; the Dockerfile's COPY of it is written to tolerate its absence. Only this one file
# is let through -- dist/ also holds the packages and the Windows exe, and a Linux server image has
# no use for either.
!dist
dist/*
!dist/H9XASH-Updater

# ---- the HD textures ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 19.7 GiB across 9,764 files (docs/HD_TEXTURES.txt). Left in, every build would spend minutes
# sending a context the image does not want, and a server has no use for them at all.
H9XASH/ts/materials

# ---- SECRETS: never in an image ------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are in the updater's SKIP_NAMES as "a player's, a server's or a secret file". They hold
# this server's own keys and addresses. Give them to a container at run time with a mount or a
# Docker secret; docs/DOCKER.txt says how. Baking one into an image and pushing it publishes it.
**/h9_presence.cfg
**/ts_advertise.cfg
**/ts_advertise_local.cfg
**/mail.env
**/accounts.json
**/listip.cfg
**/banned.cfg
**/users.ini
**/sql.cfg
**/*.env
**/*.key
**/*.pem
!H9XASH/ts/addons/amxmodx/data/amxx_easy_http_cacert.pem
!H9XASH/valve/cacert.pem
!H9XASH-linux/ts/addons/amxmodx/data/amxx_easy_http_cacert.pem

# ---- PLAYER FILES: belong to whoever runs the game -------------------------------------------------
**/user_id.ini
**/device_id.ini
**/.xash_id
**/config.cfg
**/config.cfg.bak
**/video.cfg
**/opengl.cfg
**/custom.hpk
**/voice_ban.dt
**/tempdecal.wad
**/tsstats.dat
**/vault.ini
**/bot_playerids.ini
**/console_history.txt
**/history_servers.lst
**/favorite_servers.lst
**/xashcomm.lst
**/networking.ini
**/*_resolved.cfg
**/userid_resolved.cfg

# ---- generated, transient, or a machine's own ------------------------------------------------------
**/logs
**/save
**/screenshots
**/scrshots
**/ts_downloads
**/downloads
**/.fontcache
**/userconfig.d
**/drive_c
**/dosdevices
**/presets/backup
H9XASH/ts/addons/amxmodx/data/vault
H9XASH/ts/addons/amxmodx/data/sqlite3
H9XASH/ts/addons/amxmodx/configs/precache
H9XASH/.h9xash-updater
**/*.log
**/*.pid
**/*.tmp
**/*.new
**/*.orig
**/*.rej
**/*.dmp
**/*.mdmp
**/*.dem
**/*.sav
**/thumbs.db
**/desktop.ini
**/.ds_store

# ---- WINDOWS: dead weight in a Linux server image ---------------------------------------------------
# The engine, the game library and every module in this image are i386 ELF; nothing here can load
# a PE. Leaving them in would add hundreds of megabytes that can never run.
**/*.exe
**/*.dll
**/*.bat
**/*.ps1
**/*.pdb
H9XASH/webview2
H9XASH/discord-bot
H9XASH/ts/h9tts
H9XASH/ts/cl_dlls

# ---- never useful in a build context -----------------------------------------------------------------
**/.git
**/__pycache__
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/venv
dockerfiles/server
dockerfiles/server.env
